Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:05:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FunKey S: the FunKey menu (volume, brightness, aspect ratio,
 FPS, exit game)

Menu opens a menu in the style of FunKey-OS's own emulators' menus (written for this game): one item at a time in a
light grey box over the darkened game, arrows above and below, Open Sans Bold from the firmware's menu resources (the
5x7 dots if missing), the next item sliding in at 50 pictures a second. VOLUME and BRIGHTNESS (FunKey-OS's volume and
brightness commands, one at a time, the last value in the end), ASPECT RATIO (4:3, or STRETCHED across the whole
screen), SHOW FPS (the pictures of the last second, top left), EXIT GAME ("Are you sure ?", A again). The game, its
sound (audioSetPaused) and the speaker's amplifier wait meanwhile; the game's clock skips the time spent in the menu,
and the buttons pressed reach the game only once let go. Aspect ratio and FPS are kept in isaac.ini (main.cpp's
saveIniValue, shared now). It replaces Menu pressed twice to quit. Test hooks: the test script's "menushot" and
"aspect", ISAAC_FUNKEY_MENU_RES.
